<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs - Monday estimate 105,000 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs - Monday estimate 105,000 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interior Iowa and southern Minnesota hog marketings Monday were estimated at 105,000 head compared with 116,000 a week ago and 111,000 a year ago, according to USDA.</p>
<p>Estimates include generally about 60 percent Carcass Base Hogs. Barrows and gilts were $0.50 per cwt higher than midsession Friday. Trade was slow to moderate for light demand and offerings.</p>
<p>				 Country		  Plants</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>220-260 lbs	   52.00 -53.00	   53.00 -54.00</p>
<p>few		     53.50		    54.50</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>260-280 lbs	   50.00 -53.00	   50.50 -54.00</p>
<p>US 2-4   43-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>280-300 lbs	   46.50 -51.50	   47.00 -52.50</p>
<p>Sows:  steady to $1.00 lower. US 1-3 300-450 lbs. 42.00 -45.00	   43.00 -45.00</p>
<p>450-500 lbs.	  46.00 -48.00	   46.00 -49.00</p>
<p>500 lbs. up	   47.00 -52.00	   47.00 -53.00</p>
<p>Note: Prices quoted represent sales of hogs averaging 73-74 pct. carcass yields with mostly 1.00-1.25 inches of last rib backfat and 47-48 pct. lean. Special considerations and grade premiums not reflected in base prices.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
